{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["And the reason for <b>why is it that you transgress the word of YHWH</b> is not in connection with the decree of \"in this wilderness your carcasses shall fall\" which He said (Numbers 14:29), but rather He says: why are you transgressing the word of YHWH, for He commanded me that you shall not go up at all and that you shall not be routed before your enemies. And so He said in Mishneh Torah: \"And you were contentious about going up the mountain, and YHWH said to me, say to them: Do not go up and do not fight, for I am not in your midst, and you shall not be routed before your enemies\" (Deuteronomy 1:41–42)." "And the reason for <b>and it shall not succeed</b> — that which you are doing shall not succeed, in the language of Rashi (Rashi on Numbers 14:41). Or: the transgression of the word of HaShem has no success in it, in the language of Ibn Ezra (Ibn Ezra on Numbers 14:41). And by way of truth — \"it walks\" (Ezekiel 1:13)."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:05:49.775200945Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}